*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREDENTIALS — this repository is PUBLIC and is served by GitHub Pages.
# Anything committed here is world-readable and stays in git history forever,
# even after deletion. A leaked service-account key must be revoked in GCP, not
# just removed from the tree.
# Added 2026-08-11: .gitignore previously covered only __pycache__/, while the
# panel's documented credential path is .streamlit/secrets.toml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.streamlit/secrets.toml
secrets.toml
*-service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
gcp-*.json
application_default_credentials.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# tokens seen in this project's history: Synoptic, CLOUDS, Earthdata JWT, GitHub PATs
*token*.txt
*.secret

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local artefacts
